    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "FRAMEWORK",
      "narration_text": "Ask two questions of every case: what was it really, and what did the model say? Rows hold the truth; columns hold the prediction. Agreement lands on the diagonal: true positives and true negatives. Off the diagonal sit the two mistakes. A false positive is a false alarm. A false negative is a miss.",
