    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "Now the trap. A lazy model that never flags anything scores ninety-eight percent accuracy, almost matching ours. Its matrix gives it away: zero true positives, all twenty frauds missed, recall zero. Accuracy hid that; the matrix cannot. One caution: some tools put predictions in the rows, so read the axis labels before you read a cell.",
